# Every path an install of this harness owns. install.sh reads it to decide what
# to write; update.sh reads the copy already in the project to decide what to
# delete. If a path is not in here, install does not touch it.
#
# Bump `version` whenever the set of paths changes. It is not used for
# comparison — the path lists are — but it gives a human something to point at.

version 7

# Modes
#
#   replace   Copied from the source tree on every install. Deleting the line
#             deletes the file from the project on the next `./sandbox update`.
#             This is the harness: not project code, safe to overwrite.
#
#   preserve  Copied from the source tree only when the project does not have
#             it. Never overwritten, never deleted — once it exists it is the
#             project's. (sandbox.conf is the exception that still gets the
#             incoming defaults dropped beside it as sandbox.conf.new.)
#
#   manage    Install touches it but does not own its contents: merged into,
#             generated, or purely the project's own state. Never wholesale
#             copied, never deleted. Listed so this file is the complete
#             footprint rather than most of it.

# --- the CLI and the harness ------------------------------------------------
